      "text": "To determine the area of Mateen's backyard, we need to find the length and width of the rectangular backyard. Let's denote the length of the backyard by \\( l \\) meters and the width by \\( w \\) meters.\n\nFirst, we use the information that Mateen has to walk the length 25 times to cover 1000 meters. This means that the total length of the backyard is:\n\\[\nl = 25 \\times 40 = 1000 \\text{ meters}\n\\]\n\nNext, we use the information that Mateen has to walk the perimeter 10 times to cover 1000 meters. The perimeter \\( P \\) of a rectangle is given by:\n\\[\nP = 2l + 2w\n\\]\nSince the perimeter is 1000 meters, we have:\n\\[\n2l + 2w = 1000\n\\]\nWe already know that \\( l = 1000 \\), so we substitute this into the equation for the perimeter:\n\\[\n2(1000) + 2w = 1000\n\\]\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[\n2000 + 2w = 1000\n\\]\nSubtracting 2000 from both sides gives:\n\\[\n2w = 1000 - 2000\n\\]\n\\[\n2w = 100\n\\]\nDividing both sides by 2, we get:\n\\[\nw = 50\n\\]\n\nNow that we have the length and width, we can find the area \\( A \\) of the backyard. The area of a rectangle is given by:\n\\[\nA = l \\times w\n\\]\nSubstituting the values of \\( l \\) and \\( w \\), we get:\n\\[\nA = 1000 \\times 50 = 50000 \\text{ square meters}\n\\]\n\nThus, the area of Mateen's backyard is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{50000}\n\\]",
